          "line_number": 99,
          "source": "topic-set-major-events-throughout-Paleontology-🆔20251018203122.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Ichnology:** The study of **trace fossils** (like footprints, burrows, and tooth marks), which provides a direct record of animal *behavior* rather than just their bodies.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 105,
          "source": "topic-set-major-events-throughout-Paleontology-🆔20251018203122.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Paleoclimatology:** The science of reconstructing past climates using \"proxies\" like ice cores, tree rings, and the chemical composition of marine fossils.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 107,
          "source": "topic-set-major-events-throughout-Paleontology-🆔20251018203122.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dinosaur-Bird Transition:** An exploration of the overwhelming fossil evidence (e.g., feathered dinosaurs) that reveals modern birds are the direct descendants of theropod dinosaurs.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set-major-events-throughout-Paleontology-🆔20251018203122.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stratigraphy:** The study of rock layers (strata). This is the foundational tool paleontologists use to place fossils in their correct geological order and establish a \"relative\" timeline of life on Earth.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 109,
          "source": "topic-set-major-events-throughout-Paleontology-🆔20251018203122.md"
        }
      ]
    },
